    {
      "id": "629cecef5d154299b992d9124172d751",
      "text": "Good-to-great companies have a culture of discipline",
      "source": {
        "book": "Collins-2001-Good-to-Great-Why-Some-Companies-Make-the-Leap...and-Others-Dont_",
        "chapter": 73
      },
      "weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "d1964931f8de4b9f8d639aeafb422745",
      "text": "Unsustained comparisons show that discipline is not a distinguishing variable",
      "source": {
        "book": "Collins-2001-Good-to-Great-Why-Some-Companies-Make-the-Leap...and-Others-Dont_",
        "chapter": 73
      },
      "weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "0dcfc6a01a9d417f823cd4b06c312897",
      "text": "Disciplinarian leaders can produce spectacular results but also lead to decline when they leave or become undisciplined",
      "source": {
        "book": "Collins-2001-Good-to-Great-Why-Some-Companies-Make-the-Leap...and-Others-Dont_",
        "chapter": 73
      },
      "weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "ddb363c0c67a47e99b245dfdca531378",
      "text": "Pitney Bowes' disciplined diversification led to its success",
      "source": {
        "book": "Collins-2001-Good-to-Great-Why-Some-Companies-Make-the-Leap...and-Others-Dont_",
        "chapter": 75
      },
      "weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "81e96427538244e69a32acb3f2c671f6",
      "text": "R.J. Reynolds' lack of discipline led to its failure",
      "source": {
        "book": "Collins-2001-Good-to-Great-Why-Some-Companies-Make-the-Leap...and-Others-Dont_",
        "chapter": 75
      },
      "weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "855c9c26b15749eb95496a175dc4c0a6",
      "text": "Nucor's egalitarian meritocracy was key to its success",
      "source": {
        "book": "Collins-2001-Good-to-Great-Why-Some-Companies-Make-the-Leap...and-Others-Dont_",
        "chapter": 75
      },
      "weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "d349802a35cb4d9585e9a648e60d2503",
      "text": "Nucor's unique culture and leadership approach led to its success",
      "source": {
        "book": "Collins-2001-Good-to-Great-Why-Some-Companies-Make-the-Leap...and-Others-Dont_",
        "chapter": 75
      },
      "weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "e2bd8da748954965bc71290fea757cca",
      "text": "Bethlehem Steel's focus on class distinctions and social hierarchy hindered its growth",
      "source": {
        "book": "Collins-2001-Good-to-Great-Why-Some-Companies-Make-the-Leap...and-Others-Dont_",
        "chapter": 75
      },
      "weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "2038be4512d64f8697fe3719521c8671",
      "text": "Aligning worker interests with management interests is crucial for success",
      "source": {
        "book": "Collins-2001-Good-to-Great-Why-Some-Companies-Make-the-Leap...and-Others-Dont_",
        "chapter": 75
